WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:38.769
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:39.039 --> 01:41.240
If you want to stand firm in this position,

3
01:41.759 --> 01:43.200
hard work alone

4
01:43.520 --> 01:44.800
isn't enough.

5
01:45.720 --> 01:47.479
Because everyone else works hard too.

6
01:47.840 --> 01:50.200
I'd better go get that information for Nannalin.

7
01:50.479 --> 01:51.800
Yeah, see you later.

8
01:54.120 --> 01:55.440
Your heart is beating so fast.

9
01:57.640 --> 01:59.960
I'm sorry Ratee arrived early.

10
02:00.560 --> 02:01.880
Not at all.

11
02:02.120 --> 02:03.240
It's really a pleasure.

12
02:03.240 --> 02:04.520
Please, have a seat.

13
02:05.520 --> 02:06.640
It is rather strange.

14
02:07.040 --> 02:10.120
Someone as meticulous and ambitious as Ratee...

15
02:11.120 --> 02:13.160
Why would she hire an agency like ours?

16
02:49.400 --> 02:50.880
Yes, Ms. Nannalin?

17
02:51.200 --> 02:52.720
I've arrived at the multibrand store.

18
02:53.240 --> 02:54.240
What do you see?

19
02:55.400 --> 02:57.800
Overall, it looks good. The store is beautiful.

20
02:58.120 --> 02:59.960
I'll take another look around,

21
02:59.960 --> 03:01.880
then send you my report right away.

22
03:02.520 --> 03:05.280
Pick up the items and come straight back to the office.

23
03:05.760 --> 03:06.320
Okay?

24
03:06.480 --> 03:07.320
Understood.

25
03:48.520 --> 03:50.520
Oh my goodness, Pim!

26
03:50.520 --> 03:54.320
Look at our rookie! She's all grown up now!

27
03:54.640 --> 03:56.120
You're right!

28
03:56.960 --> 03:58.760
I have to agree with Nui.

29
03:58.760 --> 04:01.400
Alice looks so much better today.

30
04:01.400 --> 04:04.680
Her scheduling and desk organization...

31
04:04.680 --> 04:07.400
She looks so professional and ready to work.

32
04:08.000 --> 04:09.240
Well done!

33
04:09.520 --> 04:11.200
Thank you, Pim and Nui.

34
04:11.200 --> 04:13.640
This time, I've made myself a promise.

35
04:13.640 --> 04:16.800
I won't be as disorganized as I was before.

36
04:16.800 --> 04:18.519
I promise I won't be disorganized again. I'm giving this my all!

37
04:19.279 --> 04:20.200
Fabulous!

38
04:20.519 --> 04:22.960
Then organize mine too, will you?

39
04:24.960 --> 04:27.120
Don't celebrate too soon, Alice.

40
04:30.840 --> 04:32.360
Remember one thing.

41
04:32.360 --> 04:33.920
In the real working world,

42
04:33.920 --> 04:36.040
work tends to come at you

43
04:36.040 --> 04:38.760
with the biggest, most urgent problems

44
04:39.320 --> 04:42.280
just when you think you have everything under control.

45
04:51.920 --> 04:53.000
Back to work, darling.

46
04:54.360 --> 04:55.200
Let's get to work.

47
05:04.760 --> 05:06.160
Get to work.

48
05:06.160 --> 05:07.840
You, darling. Get back to work.

49
05:20.240 --> 05:21.760
Your morning hot tea,

50
05:21.760 --> 05:24.440
and this week's schedule summary.

51
05:24.720 --> 05:26.520
I've organized your appointments

52
05:26.520 --> 05:29.200
and allowed time for the meetings.

53
05:50.440 --> 05:51.400
The tea is too weak.

54
05:52.200 --> 05:53.560
And the schedule is too packed.

55
05:56.040 --> 05:59.120
Oolong tea needs hotter water to steep properly.

56
06:01.040 --> 06:02.800
Otherwise, its astringent aroma won't come out.

57
06:04.160 --> 06:05.160
As for the schedule,

58
06:05.760 --> 06:09.720
you've booked three major campaign meetings back-to-back

59
06:10.960 --> 06:13.080
without giving the team any time

60
06:13.080 --> 06:15.080
to discuss potential issues.

61
06:15.720 --> 06:18.080
I wouldn't call that time management.

62
06:21.000 --> 06:23.280
I'd call it sending the team into battle unprepared.

63
06:28.320 --> 06:29.320
I'm sorry.

64
06:29.560 --> 06:31.400
I'll revise it as quickly as possible.

65
06:45.360 --> 06:47.040
Go adjust the schedule,

66
06:47.320 --> 06:49.240
and add these tasks as well.

67
06:49.760 --> 06:51.040
Review every detail of the deck

68
06:51.040 --> 06:53.800
for Ratee's cosmetics brand.

69
06:53.800 --> 06:55.960
Make sure it meets the standards we agreed on.

70
06:59.640 --> 07:02.840
And coordinate the mood and tone with the creative team.

71
07:03.080 --> 07:06.760
Shortlist some more A-list KOLs

72
07:06.760 --> 07:08.480
and add five backup names.

73
07:11.480 --> 07:15.640
I want everything on my desk before my afternoon meeting.

74
07:19.280 --> 07:20.400
Any questions?

75
07:22.160 --> 07:23.120
No.

76
07:23.280 --> 07:25.440
I'll make all the revisions perfectly.

77
07:55.400 --> 07:56.200
Alice.

78
07:57.480 --> 07:59.000
Can I ask you something?

79
07:59.320 --> 08:00.360
Well...

80
08:00.480 --> 08:03.440
Does being a content creator mean

81
08:03.520 --> 08:05.680
you have to come up with and write every word yourself?

82
08:08.840 --> 08:09.840
Of course.

83
08:10.480 --> 08:11.560
I mean...

84
08:11.800 --> 08:13.240
For content work,

85
08:13.240 --> 08:14.960
we have to do the research,

86
08:15.240 --> 08:16.840
plan out the storytelling,

87
08:18.480 --> 08:20.720
and write all the captions and articles ourselves.

88
08:22.040 --> 08:24.240
We have to make sure the brand image

89
08:24.320 --> 08:25.800
comes together perfectly.

90
08:26.920 --> 08:27.720
Ugh!

91
08:28.520 --> 08:31.560
I thought there'd be a support team to write it all.

92
08:32.480 --> 08:34.679
Writing all day sounds exhausting.

93
08:36.000 --> 08:38.840
Just staring at a screen and typing all day...

94
08:39.360 --> 08:40.159
Oh,

95
08:40.240 --> 08:41.080
how boring!

96
09:02.360 --> 09:04.560
Pim, let's go to the meeting room.

97
09:34.400 --> 09:35.200
Alice.

98
09:35.680 --> 09:36.880
Can I ask you a favor?

99
09:37.920 --> 09:38.720
Mm-hmm.

100
09:40.440 --> 09:41.320
Could you take a look...

101
09:41.440 --> 09:45.160
at my caption for the cosmetics campaign?

102
09:45.160 --> 09:47.320
I've put together a rough draft, but

103
09:47.640 --> 09:49.440
I'm not sure if it's any good.

104
10:01.120 --> 10:02.640
Here's the thing, Mueanfun.

105
10:03.160 --> 10:05.680
Ratee's cosmetics brand

106
10:05.680 --> 10:08.640
is meant to feel expensive and sophisticated.

107
10:09.040 --> 10:11.680
So the language and captions

108
10:11.880 --> 10:14.240
need to be nuanced,

109
10:14.720 --> 10:16.680
refined, and understated,

110
10:16.880 --> 10:19.000
with a sense of mature confidence.

111
10:21.560 --> 10:25.040
We can't use trendy teenage slang

112
10:25.040 --> 10:28.640
or pushy, hard-sell promotional language.

113
10:28.920 --> 10:29.960
That just won't work.

114
10:31.160 --> 10:33.840
Otherwise, everything the brand has built

115
10:33.840 --> 10:35.800
could fall apart in an instant.

116
10:37.200 --> 10:38.400
Hmm...

117
10:38.840 --> 10:41.560
I thought we'd just use words that make people buy it.

118
10:41.560 --> 10:43.240
That should be enough, really.

119
10:43.600 --> 10:45.320
Office work is so complicated.

120
11:26.720 --> 11:27.600
Isn't she kind?

121
11:29.000 --> 11:31.720
I really admire how kind Alice is.

122
11:32.080 --> 11:33.760
She's already buried in work,

123
11:34.160 --> 11:35.840
yet she still makes time

124
11:35.840 --> 11:38.280
to rescue Mueanfun's awful campaign keywords.

125
11:38.680 --> 11:39.640
That girl...

126
11:39.640 --> 11:41.200
She acts like the chairman's granddaughter.

127
11:42.080 --> 11:44.200
A high-class content creator!

128
11:44.200 --> 11:46.800
But do you know what content she watches all day?

129
11:46.800 --> 11:50.720
Online shopping! Choosing suit colors all day, swipe, swipe!

130
11:50.720 --> 11:52.200
She's been at it since nine this morning.

131
11:52.480 --> 11:53.720
Keep your voice down, Nui.

132
11:53.960 --> 11:55.960
Seriously, Nui, don't mock her so much. Someone might hear us.

133
11:56.160 --> 11:58.600
If somebody walks by and hears us,

134
11:58.840 --> 12:00.080
we'll be in trouble again.

135
12:02.880 --> 12:05.840
But your comparison was pretty accurate.

136
12:06.320 --> 12:09.000
Content in her online shopping cart!

137
12:09.440 --> 12:10.520
You're wicked!

138
12:18.440 --> 12:20.920
Being kind is a good thing, Alice.

139
12:21.560 --> 12:23.200
Helping your coworkers

140
12:23.200 --> 12:24.200
isn't wrong at all.

141
12:25.720 --> 12:28.680
But remember this important boundary.

142
12:29.200 --> 12:30.720
You can help them,

143
12:31.520 --> 12:35.480
but don't help so much that everyone at the company starts believing

144
12:35.480 --> 12:37.200
that what you're doing

145
12:37.200 --> 12:39.320
is actually your responsibility.

146
12:52.920 --> 12:54.800
As for the content section,

147
12:55.080 --> 12:56.400
I think

148
12:56.640 --> 12:59.840
we should make short, viral-style videos, like...

149
13:00.240 --> 13:01.600
the kind young people love.

150
13:01.600 --> 13:02.760
And use hashtags

151
13:03.040 --> 13:04.840
that are trending right now.

152
13:04.840 --> 13:06.080
I guarantee

153
13:06.440 --> 13:08.520
our engagement will skyrocket.

154
13:11.120 --> 13:12.000
Brilliant, right?

155
13:13.040 --> 13:13.840
Isn't it brilliant?

156
13:14.120 --> 13:14.920
It'll go through the roof!

157
13:20.000 --> 13:20.560
Well,

158
13:20.800 --> 13:22.800
what Mueanfun is suggesting

159
13:23.040 --> 13:24.240
is probably

160
13:24.240 --> 13:27.800
to use the energy of short-form video,

161
13:27.800 --> 13:31.280
but adapt the storytelling to a quiet luxury mood.

162
13:31.600 --> 13:34.440
Instead of using generic trending hashtags,

163
13:34.440 --> 13:38.640
we could focus on polished lighting and composition

164
13:38.840 --> 13:42.520
to appeal to older teens and working women

165
13:42.680 --> 13:45.000
who appreciate a premium aesthetic.

166
13:45.000 --> 13:46.720
That fits Ratee's brief perfectly.

167
13:48.400 --> 13:49.200
Exactly!

168
13:49.640 --> 13:51.440
Just like Alice said. What do you think?

169
13:51.640 --> 13:52.640
Good idea, right?

170
13:53.760 --> 13:54.560
Makes sense, doesn't it?

171
13:56.320 --> 13:57.120
It does.

172
13:57.160 --> 13:58.080
Slay, girl!

173
13:58.960 --> 13:59.760
Absolutely slay!

174
14:03.080 --> 14:03.840
What?

175
14:03.840 --> 14:05.720
I think these two are in for a long rivalry.

176
14:05.720 --> 14:07.400
They might become competitors

177
14:07.400 --> 14:10.400
for the title of our office's legendary content creator.

178
14:10.400 --> 14:12.720
right here in our office, for sure.

179
14:13.680 --> 14:15.480
Competitors? No way!

180
14:15.480 --> 14:18.640
One works so hard she can barely breathe,

181
14:18.640 --> 14:19.880
while the other

182
14:20.080 --> 14:23.600
casually picks phone case colors from her shopping cart.

183
14:25.080 --> 14:25.880
Exactly.

184
14:26.400 --> 14:27.240
Um...

185
14:27.640 --> 14:30.520
The afternoon campaign summary is done, Pim.

186
14:31.760 --> 14:33.240
Just put it down for now, Alice.

187
14:33.240 --> 14:35.040
Take a break and drink some water.

188
14:35.240 --> 14:37.600
You've been working nonstop since day one.

189
14:37.840 --> 14:42.280
Everyone here can see who's actually working.

190
14:42.400 --> 14:44.000
You don't have to push yourself so hard.

191
14:45.160 --> 14:45.960
Okay.

192
14:51.880 --> 14:52.760
Snacks!

193
14:53.640 --> 14:54.760
Thank you.

194
14:55.120 --> 14:55.800
Thanks!

195
14:57.240 --> 14:58.240
Can I have some too?

196
14:58.240 --> 14:59.600
Sharing is caring!

197
14:59.880 --> 15:01.800
You never miss a chance to eat, do you?

198
15:02.240 --> 15:04.640
Never! Eating and gossiping go hand in hand.

199
15:05.400 --> 15:06.000
Stop it!

200
15:06.000 --> 15:07.320
A break? We're allowed to rest?

201
15:07.920 --> 15:08.440
A break!

202
15:08.440 --> 15:08.960
A snack break.

203
15:09.160 --> 15:09.800
Let's work, shall we?

204
15:09.800 --> 15:10.200
Okay.

205
15:10.200 --> 15:10.600
Sure.

206
15:11.520 --> 15:12.560
Can I have one?

207
15:13.160 --> 15:13.680
Just one!

208
15:14.880 --> 15:15.680
Sure.

209
15:37.000 --> 15:38.600
Do you have that much free time, Alice?

210
15:39.520 --> 15:40.320
Sorry?

211
15:40.840 --> 15:42.720
Why are you doing someone else's work?

212
15:45.760 --> 15:46.800
Um...

213
15:47.320 --> 15:48.200
Well...

214
15:57.240 --> 15:58.040
It's fine to be kind,

215
16:00.920 --> 16:02.840
but you're not being very smart.

216
16:26.680 --> 16:28.680
Alice, we're heading home.

217
16:29.400 --> 16:30.440
Okay, bye-bye!

218
16:31.120 --> 16:31.920
Bye!

219
16:31.920 --> 16:32.720
Bye-bye!

220
16:52.160 --> 16:53.360
Alice!

221
16:54.240 --> 16:56.360
Fun needs another favor.

222
16:56.760 --> 17:00.360
I didn't understand the campaign from this afternoon.

223
17:00.600 --> 17:03.240
And I have to rush to dinner with my family.

224
17:03.480 --> 17:05.480
If I sit here trying to work it out alone,

225
17:05.680 --> 17:08.520
I'll be late and get scolded for sure.

226
17:09.319 --> 17:10.400
Well, actually...

227
17:11.640 --> 17:15.839
I still haven't finished rescheduling our meetings

228
17:15.839 --> 17:17.319
or compiling the KOL list.

229
17:17.960 --> 17:20.359
Come on, please help me.

230
17:20.359 --> 17:21.720
It's just a little thing.

231
17:21.920 --> 17:24.920
You can fix something this simple in no time, Alice.

232
17:24.920 --> 17:27.240
I've already shared the file to your computer.

233
17:27.240 --> 17:30.040
I've got to go. Thanks, Alice! I'm counting on you!

234
17:51.920 --> 17:52.720
Hey!

235
17:53.760 --> 17:54.560
What is this?

236
17:57.520 --> 17:59.880
The copy for the cosmetics campaign...

237
18:00.200 --> 18:01.160
The content section?

238
18:02.120 --> 18:03.840
You're doing someone else's work again, aren't you?

239
18:05.680 --> 18:06.480
Yeah.

240
18:09.080 --> 18:10.880
But if I don't fix it,

241
18:11.520 --> 18:12.640
this whole project will be a disaster.

242
18:14.040 --> 18:16.880
I can't just stand by and watch it fall apart.

243
18:18.920 --> 18:19.720
Listen.

244
18:21.960 --> 18:23.160
And if you're the one who falls apart,

245
18:23.400 --> 18:24.360
who's going to help you?

246
18:26.280 --> 18:28.360
I know you're new here,

247
18:28.720 --> 18:30.560
and you want to prove yourself.

248
18:31.280 --> 18:33.320
But your kindness

249
18:33.560 --> 18:35.080
is only going to ruin you.

250
18:35.400 --> 18:36.080
Do you understand?

251
18:38.800 --> 18:39.600
Now eat your dinner.

252
18:40.000 --> 18:41.040
Can't I just finish a little more?

253
18:41.040 --> 18:41.600
Hmph.

254
18:42.240 --> 18:43.040
That's enough.

255
18:53.440 --> 18:54.240
Hey!

256
18:55.360 --> 18:56.200
What the hell?

257
18:56.200 --> 18:57.280
You look like you've seen a ghost.

258
18:58.640 --> 18:59.880
It's Nannalin!

259
19:00.120 --> 19:00.760
What about her?

260
19:01.680 --> 19:03.040
She told me to come to her house.

261
19:03.800 --> 19:04.600
Holy crap!

262
19:05.200 --> 19:06.080
Don't say that!

263
19:07.200 --> 19:09.160
Is she going to yell at me?

264
19:09.600 --> 19:10.520
You're so screwed.

265
19:12.560 --> 19:13.360
Huh?

266
19:13.960 --> 19:15.760
I really don't want to go.

267
19:29.880 --> 19:32.400
I'm just dropping off work, Alice.

268
19:32.840 --> 19:33.960
It's no big deal.

269
20:12.560 --> 20:13.800
Come upstairs.

270
20:14.880 --> 20:16.560
Or do I have to go down and get you myself?

271
20:45.800 --> 20:47.040
Um...

272
20:47.960 --> 20:51.440
Does your house normally look like this, Ms. Nannalin?

273
20:52.120 --> 20:54.680
If I wasted all my time doing housework,

274
20:54.680 --> 20:56.360
who would do tomorrow's work?

275
21:04.080 --> 21:04.880
And...

276
21:05.080 --> 21:07.280
Aren't you going to...

277
21:07.640 --> 21:09.400
clean up a little?

278
21:10.360 --> 21:13.680
My regular housekeeper had to take sudden leave to go upcountry.

279
21:17.120 --> 21:18.680
Don't look at me like that.

280
21:25.600 --> 21:27.040
Just give me the documents.

281
23:02.840 --> 23:03.640
Alice.

282
23:05.760 --> 23:07.440
You really don't have to do that.

283
23:08.600 --> 23:09.920
It's not your job.

284
23:11.760 --> 23:12.640
It's okay.

285
23:28.080 --> 23:30.520
Who drinks this much tea every day?

286
23:31.280 --> 23:33.600
It keeps me from murdering people in meetings.

287
23:38.280 --> 23:40.640
Then please drink plenty of it.

288
24:30.640 --> 24:32.560
You're this flustered just seeing my underwear.

289
24:47.120 --> 24:48.560
If you saw me wearing it,

290
24:48.840 --> 24:51.200
would you have a heart attack, Alice?

291
25:15.880 --> 25:16.680
Am I beautiful?

292
25:19.760 --> 25:20.560
Yes, you are.

293
25:24.920 --> 25:26.200
If I'm that beautiful,

294
25:28.920 --> 25:30.320
are you just going to stand there?

295
25:34.320 --> 25:35.880
I don't want to just stand here.

296
32:11.360 --> 32:12.240
Tomorrow,

297
32:12.440 --> 32:15.160
don't take on Mueanfun's work again.

298
32:15.840 --> 32:18.240
I hired you to be my assistant,

299
32:19.240 --> 32:20.960
not a dumping ground

300
32:21.080 --> 32:22.920
for other people's responsibilities.

301
32:31.440 --> 32:32.520
If you do it again,

302
32:34.440 --> 32:35.280
I'll be angry.

303
32:43.880 --> 32:44.840
Okay.

304
32:46.040 --> 32:47.520
And next time,

305
32:48.640 --> 32:50.760
if you're going to tidy up my house again,

306
32:52.120 --> 32:53.720
ask for permission first.

307
33:14.600 --> 33:16.440
Do I need to resign now?

308
33:18.360 --> 33:18.840
No!

309
33:18.960 --> 33:19.800
I can't!

310
33:20.360 --> 33:23.040
I haven't even been here a month!

311
33:23.920 --> 33:27.120
I can't lose my head just because my boss is so charming!

312
33:56.800 --> 33:58.760
Okay, Namhom, one more shot!

313
33:58.760 --> 34:01.360
Sexy and confident. Ready?

314
34:01.600 --> 34:03.160
One, two, three!

315
34:03.640 --> 34:05.200
Okay, beautiful!

316
34:05.200 --> 34:06.720
Let's shoot one vertically.

317
34:08.120 --> 34:10.000
Okay, one more!

318
34:10.400 --> 34:11.880
Ready? Okay!

319
34:11.880 --> 34:14.320
Beautiful, Namhom!

320
34:14.480 --> 34:17.120
Crew, let's take five to reset the lights.

321
34:23.560 --> 34:24.480
Hello!

322
34:27.440 --> 34:30.920
That was amazing! I recorded it. Look!

323
34:31.360 --> 34:32.800
Here's some cold water.

324
34:33.199 --> 34:34.600
Um, excuse me.

325
34:34.800 --> 34:36.400
For Namhom's water,

326
34:36.400 --> 34:38.920
could we have it at room temperature instead?

327
34:38.920 --> 34:41.199
Water this cold

328
34:41.199 --> 34:43.320
could dry out her throat. Of course.

329
34:43.520 --> 34:44.520
Of course!

330
34:45.880 --> 34:47.159
Hey, crew!

331
34:47.159 --> 34:49.480
Please bring her some room-temperature water.

332
34:50.560 --> 34:52.960
Anything's fine. I'm easygoing.

333
34:55.120 --> 34:56.120
And one more thing...

334
34:56.400 --> 34:58.240
Those flashes were really bright.

335
34:58.440 --> 35:00.520
They must have hurt her eyes.

336
35:00.960 --> 35:02.920
Could she rest her eyes for two minutes?

337
35:03.120 --> 35:04.000
No problem.

338
35:04.120 --> 35:05.760
And could we get a towel to dab her sweat?

339
35:05.760 --> 35:07.320
An ultra-soft one, please.

340
35:07.320 --> 35:10.120
Could you use a super-soft towel to dab the sweat along her hairline?

341
35:10.480 --> 35:12.240
Because regular tissues

342
35:12.480 --> 35:13.920
could irritate her face.

343
35:13.920 --> 35:15.360
Anything is fine, really.

344
35:15.760 --> 35:16.480
I'm easygoing.

345
35:16.480 --> 35:16.960
Um...

346
35:16.960 --> 35:19.440
Sorry for making you all run around so much.

347
35:19.440 --> 35:20.960
It's been a tiring day.

348
35:21.440 --> 35:23.040
After we finish this set,

349
35:23.040 --> 35:26.040
I'll treat the whole crew to bubble tea!

350
35:26.040 --> 35:26.600
How does that sound?

351
35:26.800 --> 35:28.560
It's no trouble at all.

352
35:28.560 --> 35:33.400
I'll find you an extra-soft towel.

353
35:34.080 --> 35:36.320
Anything is fine! I'm easygoing.

354
35:36.760 --> 35:37.960
Really, anything is fine.

355
35:38.240 --> 35:39.040
Thank you.

356
35:39.840 --> 35:40.920
Shall we take a picture?

357
35:42.080 --> 35:42.880
Of course!

358
36:06.200 --> 36:07.040
Oh my gosh!

359
36:07.240 --> 36:09.280
Look at her glow, Pim!

360
36:09.440 --> 36:11.440
She's so gorgeous and adorable.

361
36:12.000 --> 36:14.040
She's a star with real magnetism,

362
36:14.240 --> 36:16.880
the kind that makes people open their wallets

363
36:17.080 --> 36:18.760
even when they weren't planning to spend a thing.

364
36:19.760 --> 36:21.040
Well, obviously!

365
36:21.240 --> 36:22.960
Why else would Ratee

366
36:23.160 --> 36:28.360
pick Namhom as a top candidate for the new cosmetics campaign?

367
36:29.200 --> 36:30.360
It's a high-end brand.

368
36:30.360 --> 36:33.440
They need someone with a premium image like hers.

369
36:35.760 --> 36:36.640
Nui!

370
36:36.840 --> 36:37.400
Tone it down.

371
36:37.760 --> 36:39.000
Keep up appearances!

372
36:39.240 --> 36:40.720
Other staff might see you

373
36:40.720 --> 36:41.560
and start gossiping.

374
36:41.720 --> 36:42.840
I don't care!

375
36:43.240 --> 36:44.280
Alice, look!

376
36:44.520 --> 36:46.000
She's beautiful and adorable.

377
36:46.000 --> 36:47.600
Put her next to the product,

378
36:47.800 --> 36:49.040
and it'll practically sell itself.

379
36:49.240 --> 36:51.000
We wouldn't even need to push the content.

380
36:52.280 --> 36:53.560
She really is beautiful and cute.

381
36:54.160 --> 36:54.760
Right?

382
36:55.000 --> 36:56.360
I'm a huge fan of hers!

383
36:56.360 --> 36:57.440
I've never been to a fan meeting,

384
36:57.440 --> 36:59.960
but I won't miss the next one.

385
37:02.040 --> 37:04.000
Look at her! See what I mean?

386
37:06.320 --> 37:07.600
Namhom is...

387
37:08.200 --> 37:08.880
quite pretty.

388
37:09.840 --> 37:10.200
But...

389
37:10.200 --> 37:11.040
I think...

390
37:11.040 --> 37:13.520
her eyes look a little empty.

391
37:18.000 --> 37:19.320
You have a point, Fun.

392
37:19.720 --> 37:22.000
A lot of people online say

393
37:22.000 --> 37:23.640
Namhom is beautiful,

394
37:23.840 --> 37:24.960
but not very smart.

395
37:25.480 --> 37:26.280
I mean,

396
37:26.520 --> 37:28.640
her product reviews all seem fake.

397
37:28.640 --> 37:32.440
And at events, she can never explain the products well.

398
37:32.840 --> 37:34.160
All she has going for her is her looks.

399
37:39.280 --> 37:41.040
Yeah, yeah, okay!

400
37:41.880 --> 37:43.040
Forget what people online say.

401
37:43.040 --> 37:43.960
Let people online say what they want.

402
37:45.000 --> 37:46.040
Let's focus on our own work.

403
37:48.240 --> 37:49.400
Hey, you guys!

404
37:49.920 --> 37:52.880
The other campaign sections due this afternoon...

405
37:53.200 --> 37:54.640
have you checked them yet?

406
37:54.840 --> 37:55.520
The campaign?

407
37:55.840 --> 37:57.360
Right, the campaign. Check!

408
37:57.600 --> 37:59.520
For the presenter section,

409
37:59.520 --> 38:00.760
I'd like to propose

410
38:00.760 --> 38:02.840
Namhom as our main candidate.

411
38:03.040 --> 38:04.080
She's beautiful,

412
38:04.240 --> 38:05.200
adorable,

413
38:05.600 --> 38:07.680
and has a strong fanbase.

414
38:08.240 --> 38:10.520
Our engagement and sales

415
38:10.520 --> 38:12.720
will definitely exceed all targets.

416
38:18.680 --> 38:19.440
Her image

417
38:19.440 --> 38:21.440
and fanbase numbers look good.

418
38:23.400 --> 38:24.680
But if the public sees Namhom

419
38:24.680 --> 38:26.840
as just a pretty face

420
38:27.080 --> 38:28.080
who doesn't know much

421
38:29.320 --> 38:31.200
or can't explain product ingredients,

422
38:31.200 --> 38:32.640
as the rumors suggest,

423
38:33.120 --> 38:34.400
how will the brand respond

424
38:34.400 --> 38:36.200
and repair that perception?

425
38:53.920 --> 38:55.440
Since there's a weakness,

426
38:56.800 --> 38:58.640
I'd like to propose Prem as well,

427
38:59.160 --> 39:01.760
a rising beauty blogger.

428
39:02.800 --> 39:05.240
She has extensive cosmetics knowledge

429
39:06.040 --> 39:07.640
and a loyal following

430
39:08.120 --> 39:10.240
that really trusts what she says.

431
39:14.160 --> 39:16.160
Even though she has some online controversies

432
39:16.440 --> 39:18.640
for being outspoken,

433
39:19.040 --> 39:20.280
overconfident,

434
39:21.200 --> 39:23.480
and sometimes arguing with netizens.

435
39:24.560 --> 39:27.280
Prem has what Namhom lacks.

436
39:27.680 --> 39:29.560
Namhom has star appeal,

437
39:30.080 --> 39:32.080
while Prem has credibility.

438
39:33.240 --> 39:35.640
Putting them together in one campaign

439
39:35.640 --> 39:37.600
would give Ratee's cosmetics both emotion and reason.

440
39:37.600 --> 39:39.000
Both emotion

441
39:39.800 --> 39:42.040
and reason in perfect balance.

442
39:45.920 --> 39:46.920
Then how about

443
39:47.400 --> 39:48.640
we keep it simple?

444
39:48.760 --> 39:49.680
I think

445
39:49.920 --> 39:51.440
we should just have Prem

446
39:51.720 --> 39:54.720
explain all the product benefits,

447
39:54.720 --> 39:56.720
and Namhom can

448
39:57.520 --> 39:58.520
just sit there...

449
39:58.880 --> 40:00.760
and smile beautifully,

450
40:00.920 --> 40:03.880
while holding the product beside her.

451
40:04.200 --> 40:05.280
Easy enough, right?

452
40:08.200 --> 40:09.280
If even we,

453
40:09.360 --> 40:11.560
as the agency designing this campaign,

454
40:11.960 --> 40:14.160
see our presenter so superficially,

455
40:15.280 --> 40:16.440
the audience will think

456
40:16.520 --> 40:18.000
and see her the same way.

457
40:41.040 --> 40:42.720
If the real Namhom

458
40:42.960 --> 40:44.480
isn't intelligent

459
40:44.480 --> 40:46.360
and knows nothing about the product,

460
40:46.480 --> 40:47.760
that would be really hard for her.

461
40:48.080 --> 40:50.800
But Namhom works harder than most people think.

462
40:51.000 --> 40:51.880
How would you know?

463
40:52.160 --> 40:52.840
Unless...

464
40:53.760 --> 40:55.120
Hello, everyone!

465
40:55.720 --> 40:57.160
Namhom is here!

466
40:58.720 --> 40:59.880
Ms. Namhom

467
41:00.120 --> 41:01.440
seems to listen to you.

468
41:01.920 --> 41:03.400
Maybe it's because I

469
41:03.640 --> 41:05.240
explain things directly

470
41:05.320 --> 41:06.760
and give easy-to-follow briefs.

471
41:07.200 --> 41:08.840
You're really bad at lying, aren't you?

472
41:09.360 --> 41:11.000
You're good at comforting the presenter.
